-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles level data produce a patching datum
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a noetherian local ring that is complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $p$ be a prime with $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, let $r\in\mathbb N$, let $R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra and $M$ an $R$-module. Suppose given exponents $k(n,i)\in\mathbb N$ with $n\le k(n,i)$ for all $n$ and all $i\in\mathrm{Fin}\,r$; write $\Delta_n=\prod_{i}\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb Z/p^{k(n,i)})$. Suppose given for each $n$: a noetherian local $\mathcal O$-algebra $R_n$, a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\gamma_n\colon \mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]\to R_n$ from the multivariate power series ring on $\mathrm{Fin}\,r$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\iota_n\colon \mathcal O[\Delta_n]\to R_n$ from the monoid algebra, and a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varepsilon_n\colon R_n\to R$ with $\varepsilon_n(\iota_n(g))=1$ for every $g\in\Delta_n$; an $R_n$-module $M_n$, a number $d_n$ and elements $b_{n,1},\dots,b_{n,d_n}\in M_n$ such that every $x\in M_n$ can be written $x=\sum_i \iota_n(c_i)\cdot b_{n,i}$ with $c_i\in\mathcal O[\Delta_n]$, and such a combination vanishes exactly when all $c_i=0$; and an additive surjection $\lambda_n\colon M_n\to M$ with $\lambda_n(x\cdot m)=\varepsilon_n(x)\cdot\lambda_n(m)$ whose kernel consists of the elements of $(\iota_n(\ker \text{counit}))\cdot M_n$, the counit being the bialgebra counit of $\mathcal O[\Delta_n]$. Then the type $\mathtt{Algebra.PatchingDatum}\ \mathcal O\ p\ r\ R\ M$ is nonempty: there is a family, indexed by $n\in\mathbb N$, of patching levels for the ideal $J_n=\big((1+X_j)^{p^n}-1 : j\in\mathrm{Fin}\,r\big)$ of $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$, each consisting of an $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$-module $N$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$, a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi\colon\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]\to R$ with $\psi(\varphi(X_i))=0$ for all $i$, an additive surjection $\pi\colon N\to M$ with $\pi(f\cdot x)=\psi(f)\cdot\pi(x)$ and kernel the submodule $(\varphi(X_1),\dots,\varphi(X_r))\cdot N$, together with a number $d$ and elements $b_1,\dots,b_d\in N$ such that every $x\in N$ is of the form $\sum_i\varphi(c_i)\cdot b_i$ and such a combination vanishes exactly when every $c_i$ lies in $J_n$.
--
--   This is the purely algebraic step that converts the output of a Taylor–Wiles system — a tower of augmented diamond-ring level data $(R_n,\iota_n,\varepsilon_n,M_n,\lambda_n)$ with $M_n$ free over $\mathcal O[\Delta_n]$ — into a patching datum in the sense used by the patching argument, by transporting the group-algebra structure to power series via surjections $\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]\to\mathcal O[\Delta_n]$ with kernel $\big((1+X_j)^{p^{k(n,j)}}-1\big)$. No condition relating $R_n$ to a deformation ring is imposed beyond surjectivity of $\varepsilon_n$ and the triviality of $\varepsilon_n\circ\iota_n$. It is invoked by [`Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_flatLevelTower`](thm.html#Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_flatLevelTower) and [`Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_strictOrdinaryLevelTower`](thm.html#Algebra.nonempty_patchingDatum_of_strictOrdinaryLevelTower).
